From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pkgdemon <jpm820@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:26:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] NextBSD: Linuxulator: let pread64 work on memfd and shm
 descriptors

linux_pread() did the read with kern_pread() and only then called
fgetvp() on the descriptor to return EISDIR for a directory. fgetvp()
returns EINVAL for any file without a vnode (kern_descrip.c
_fgetvp()), so pread64 on a memfd, which is a DTYPE_SHM file with
f_vnode == NULL, copied the data into the caller's buffer and then
failed with EINVAL. A glibc loader reading a library from a memfd
fails with "cannot read file data: Invalid argument".

Do the directory check before the read, and only for files that have
a vnode. Non-seekable files (pipes, sockets, FIFOs) still get ESPIPE
from kern_preadv(), as on Linux.

Fixes: nextbsd/nextbsd#512

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/compat/linux/linux_file.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/compat/linux/linux_file.c b/sys/compat/linux/linux_file.c
index 84ef3461e..d39fc9c71 100644
--- a/sys/compat/linux/linux_file.c
+++ b/sys/compat/linux/linux_file.c
@@ -1025,7 +1025,7 @@ linux_sync_file_range(struct thread *td, struct linux_sync_file_range_args *uap)
 int
 linux_pread(struct thread *td, struct linux_pread_args *uap)
 {
-	struct vnode *vp;
+	struct file *fp;
 	off_t offset;
 	int error;
 
@@ -1035,17 +1035,23 @@ linux_pread(struct thread *td, struct linux_pread_args *uap)
 	offset = uap->offset;
 #endif
 
-	error = kern_pread(td, uap->fd, uap->buf, uap->nbyte, offset);
-	if (error == 0) {
-		/* This seems to violate POSIX but Linux does it. */
-		error = fgetvp(td, uap->fd, &cap_pread_rights, &vp);
-		if (error != 0)
-			return (error);
-		if (vp->v_type == VDIR)
-			error = EISDIR;
-		vrele(vp);
-	}
-	return (error);
+	/*
+	 * Linux fails pread(2) on a directory with EISDIR, which can differ
+	 * from our behaviour when reading directories is allowed.  Check
+	 * before the read, and only for descriptors backed by a vnode:
+	 * memfd and other shm descriptors have no vnode, are seekable and
+	 * must be preadable as on Linux.
+	 */
+	error = fget(td, uap->fd, &cap_pread_rights, &fp);
+	if (error != 0)
+		return (error);
+	if (fp->f_vnode != NULL && fp->f_vnode->v_type == VDIR)
+		error = EISDIR;
+	fdrop(fp, td);
+	if (error != 0)
+		return (error);
+
+	return (kern_pread(td, uap->fd, uap->buf, uap->nbyte, offset));
 }
 
 int
